From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:44:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: sn201202x: wait for the role switch before
 waking

tipd_init() defers until the connector's USB role switch (the dwc3) is
registered, but only after it has woken the chip, switched it to S0
and set its interrupt mask, and the deferral then puts the chip back
to sleep. With both drivers loaded by udev at boot that cycle could
repeat several times. Look the role switch up in sn201202x_probe() and
defer there instead, before the chip is touched. A connector without a
role switch, or one whose remote node is disabled, gives NULL and the
probe continues as before.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 2ec9d7ec4317d89dcb5eb8d299eece6b1b0860b1)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
index e24ada69cf..144a4787c5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
@@ -5,8 +5,10 @@
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
 #include <linux/of_irq.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/spmi.h>
+#include <linux/usb/role.h>
 
 #include "tps6598x.h"
 
@@ -209,6 +211,8 @@ static int sn201202x_probe(struct spmi_device *device)
 {
 	const struct of_device_id *match;
 	const struct tipd_data *data;
+	struct usb_role_switch *sw;
+	struct fwnode_handle *fwnode;
 	struct sn201202x *sn;
 	struct tps6598x *tps;
 	int irq_select, irq_sleep, irq_wake;
@@ -219,6 +223,22 @@ static int sn201202x_probe(struct spmi_device *device)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	data = tipd_hw_variants[(enum tipd_hw_variant)match->data];
 
+	/*
+	 * tipd_init() defers until the connector's USB role switch (the dwc3)
+	 * is registered, but only after it has woken the chip, switched it to
+	 * S0 and set its interrupt mask, and the deferral then puts the chip
+	 * back to sleep. With both drivers loaded by udev at boot that cycle
+	 * could repeat several times. Defer here instead, before the chip is
+	 * touched. A connector without a role switch, or one whose remote node
+	 * is disabled, gives NULL, and the probe continues as before.
+	 */
+	fwnode = device_get_named_child_node(&device->dev, "connector");
+	sw = fwnode_usb_role_switch_get(fwnode);
+	fwnode_handle_put(fwnode);
+	if (IS_ERR(sw))
+		return dev_err_probe(&device->dev, PTR_ERR(sw), "waiting for the USB role switch\n");
+	usb_role_switch_put(sw);
+
 	sn = devm_kzalloc(&device->dev, data->tps_struct_size, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!sn)
 		return -ENOMEM;
